## (5) OFFLINE POSITIVE CONTROL (Linux host, no crash — sequence runs to completion)

Native test step `c2_diag_tests` (build.zig:123) runs the SAME c2_diag_sequence against the
real vendored QuickJS; on this host JS_NewRuntime2 returns, so the allocator tags keep landing:

    enter heap_ok alloc_ok free_ok new_rt MMMMMMMMrt=0x31b2648 opaque_ok limits_ok new_raw RFraw_ok new_diag RFFRFRFdiag_rc=0 ctx=0x31bb678

Reading: alive, `new_rt ` is followed by 8 `M` (capped at MF_TAG_CAP) then `rt=`. This is what makes
the live `new_rt MMM` interpretable — it is NOT "instrumentation failed to compile in".

## (6) LIVE DYING SHOT — the one dispatch (C:\temp\c2_task5_init.py C:\temp\sqjs_mf.dll)

Key lines, verbatim (full driver stdout is what was captured):

    [task5] C2Sanity == 42, game alive — init dispatch authorized
