## (7) reading

    offline alive : new_rt MMMMMMMM rt=    (≥8 mallocs through mf, then returns)
    live dying    : new_rt MMM               (3 mallocs through mf, then reads die at 1851.7ms, no rt=)

JS_NewRuntime2 reached our allocator THREE times before the host went unreadable. That excludes §40's
reading (a) ("died in the QuickJS prologue before the first allocation") — the mf is demonstrably driven
and returning. It is reading (b): the death is INSIDE JS_NewRuntime2 after the 3rd mf heap_malloc, before
the call returns. It is NOT reading (c) — rt= never appeared, so §40's JS_NewRuntime2 target reproduces.

Honest boundary: this does NOT make JS_NewRuntime2 survive. rc=3 is the PROCESS exit code, not a step
code (the WARNING + §38.5 retraction apply — not "the Date intrinsic"). "Stopped after 3 M" is a position,
not a cause; §41 writes where, not why. C2 stays blocked. Single dispatch, no re-fire.

